# Sample 13 — Per-quantity voltage (`@ X kV`)
#
# A single diagram-wide `voltage` assumes every criterion is measured
# at the same busbar — not true across a transformer. Any kVA/MVA
# quantity can instead carry its own `@ X kV`, converted with THAT
# voltage regardless of what (if anything) a `voltage` statement
# declares. No `voltage` statement is needed here at all: every MVA
# quantity, including the selected setting, supplies its own.

diagram "Transformer feeder — mixed voltage levels" {
  ct 300/1 A
  show current, mva, secondary

  below "11 kV side emergency load" must 50 MVA @ 11 kV margin 10%
  above "33 kV side minimum fault" must 300 MVA @ 33 kV margin 10%

  selected "Setting" 80 MVA @ 11 kV
}
